<header><p class="st-kicker">tribal confederation · Germany and Central Europe</p><h1 class="st-title">Boii</h1><p class="st-meta">400 BCE – 40 BCE (approx.)</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A powerful Celtic people of central Europe whose name survives in 'Bohemia', builders of large fortified towns before Dacian and Germanic pressure broke them.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>The <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/boii-400">Boii</a> were a Celtic people of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/la-tene-culture">La Tène culture</a> who appear in written sources from the 4th century BCE. One branch settled in the Po valley of northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a>, where it fought <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a> until defeated in 191 BCE; another held <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/kingdom-of-bohemia">Bohemia</a> and spread along the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/danube">Danube</a> into what is now <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/austria">Austria</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/slovakia">Slovakia</a> and western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hungary">Hungary</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Like other late Celtic peoples, the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/boii-400">Boii</a> lived in a world of chieftains, warrior elites and druids. They built oppida, large fortified towns such as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zavist">Závist</a> near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/prague">Prague</a> and the settlement at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bratislava">Bratislava</a>, where they minted <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/silver">silver</a> coins, some bearing the name <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/biatec">Biatec</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iron-technology">Ironworking</a>, glass bracelets and long-distance trade with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mediterranean">Mediterranean</a> world marked their prosperity in the 2nd and 1st centuries BCE.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>Around 60 BCE the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/boii-400">Boii</a> were crushed by the Dacian king <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/burebista">Burebista</a>, and part of the people joined the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/helvetii">Helvetii</a> in their failed migration of 58 BCE. Germanic <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/marcomanni">Marcomanni</a> later occupied <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/kingdom-of-bohemia">Bohemia</a>, but the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/latin">Latin</a> name <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/boiohaemum">Boiohaemum</a>, 'home of the Boii', lives on as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bohemia">Bohemia</a>, and possibly in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bavaria">Bavaria</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="tribal confederation, 400 BCE – 40 BCE (approx.)"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><ellipse cx="44" cy="56" rx="16" ry="24"/><path d="M44 34 V78"/><path d="M68 20 V84"/><path d="M68 20 L63 30 H73 Z"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">tribal confederation</p><p class="st-emblem-region">Germany and Central Europe</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:51.74%;width:7.16%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>400 BCE – 40 BCE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/5th-century-bce">5th century BCE</a> – <a href="/centuries/1st-century-bce">1st century BCE</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>tribal confederation</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>tribal</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Critasirus</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Celtic polytheism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Gaulish (Continental Celtic)</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/czech-republic">Czech Republic</a>, <a href="/countries/austria">Austria</a>, <a href="/countries/slovakia">Slovakia</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Boii of Bohemia</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=-220&amp;focus=boii" aria-label="Boii on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5033 442 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: w